1. The number of equilateral triangles that can be formed by three vertices of a cube is
(A) 4 ;
(B) 8 ;
(C) 12 ;
(D) 24 .

Three customers are at the hairdresser's, each paying their bill at the cash register.

- the first customer pays the same amount that is in the cash register and takes out 10 reais as change;
- the second customer performs the same operation as the first;
- the third customer performs the same operation as the first two.

Find the initial amount that was in the cash register, knowing that at the end of the three operations the cash register is empty.

\section*{Task 1 - 191021}

A rectangular picture, whose side lengths are in the ratio \(2: 3\), is to receive a frame of uniform width, whose area is as large as that of the picture.

Determine all values of the ratio of the lengths of the outer edges of the frame that satisfy this requirement!

$8 \cdot 74$ Find the value of the smallest term in the following sequence:
$$a_{1}=1993^{1994^{1995}}, a_{n+1}=\left\{\begin{array}{ll}
\frac{1}{2} a_{n}, & \text { if } a_{n} \text { is even, } \\
a_{n}+7, & \text { if } a_{n} \text { is odd. }
\end{array}\right.$$

2. Given a regular triangular prism $A B C-A^{\prime} B^{\prime} C^{\prime}$, points $D$ and $E$ are on the side edges $B B^{\prime}$ and $C C^{\prime}$ respectively, and $E C=B C=2 B D$. A section is made through $A$, $D$, and $E$. If $A A^{\prime}=2 A B$,
(1) find the angle between the section and the base;
(2) find the volume ratio of the two parts the section divides the prism into.

