Example 2 (2002 Shanghai Mathematics Competition) Given that the sequences $\left\{a_{n}\right\},\left\{b_{n}\right\}$ are both arithmetic sequences, $S_{n}=a_{1}+a_{2}+\cdots+a_{n}, T_{n}=b_{1}+b_{2}+\cdots+b_{n}$, and for all positive integers $n, \frac{S_{n}}{T_{n}}=\frac{3 n+31}{31 n+3}$.
(1) Find the value of $\frac{b_{28}}{a_{28}}$;
(2) Find all positive integers $n$ such that $\frac{b_{n}}{a_{n}}$ is an integer.

Example 2 Let the set $A=\{1,2, \cdots, 366\}$. If a binary subset $B=\{a, b\}$ of $A$ satisfies $17 \mid(a+b)$, then $B$ is said to have property $P$.
(1) Find the number of binary subsets of $A$ that have property $P$;
(2) The number of a set of binary subsets of $A$, which are pairwise disjoint and have property $P$, is how many?

1. If $|-a|>-a$, then
(A) $a>0$;
(B) $a<0$;
(C) $a<-1$;
(D) $-1<a<0$;
(E) None of the above conclusions is correct.

1. Find all triples $(f, g, h)$ of injective functions from the set of real numbers to itself satisfying
$$
\begin{aligned}
f(x+f(y)) & =g(x)+h(y) \\
g(x+g(y)) & =h(x)+f(y) \\
h(x+h(y)) & =f(x)+g(y)
\end{aligned}
$$
for all real numbers $x$ and $y$. (We say a function $F$ is injective if $F(a) \neq F(b)$ for any distinct real numbers $a$ and $b$.)
Proposed by Evan Chen.

Let $T=TNFTPP$.  Points $A$ and $B$ lie on a circle centered at $O$ such that $\angle AOB$ is right.  Points $C$ and $D$ lie on radii $OA$ and $OB$ respectively such that $AC = T-3$, $CD = 5$, and $BD = 6$.  Determine the area of quadrilateral $ACDB$.

[asy]
draw(circle((0,0),10));
draw((0,10)--(0,0)--(10,0)--(0,10));
draw((0,3)--(4,0));
label("O",(0,0),SW);
label("C",(0,3),W);
label("A",(0,10),N);
label("D",(4,0),S);
label("B",(10,0),E);
[/asy]

[b]Note: This is part of the Ultimate Problem, where each question depended on the previous question.  For those who wanted to try the problem separately, [hide=here's the value of T]$T=10$[/hide].

11. (20 points) Let the function $f(x)=a x^{3}+b x^{2}+c x+d$ have an image $\Gamma$ with two extremum points $P$ and $Q$, where $P$ is the origin.
(1) When point $Q(1,2)$, find the analytical expression of $f(x)$;
(2) When point $Q$ is on the circle $C:(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=1$, find the maximum value of the slope of the tangent line to the curve $\Gamma$.

\section*{Problem 3 - 061213}

In a rectangular box with internal dimensions \(10 \mathrm{~cm}, 10 \mathrm{~cm}\) and \(1 \mathrm{~cm}\), identical spheres with a diameter of \(1 \mathrm{~cm}\) are to be placed. Someone claims that more than 105 of these spheres can fit into the box.

Determine whether this claim is correct!

2. $P Q$ is any chord passing through the focus of the parabola $y^{2}=2 p x$, $M N$ is the projection of $P Q$ on the directrix $l$, the surface area of the solid of revolution obtained by rotating $P Q$ around $l$ is $S_{1}$, and the surface area of the sphere with diameter $M N$ is $S_{2}$. Among the following conclusions, the correct one is
(A) $S_{1}>S_{2}$;
(B) $S_{1}<S_{2}$;
(C) $S_{1}=S_{2}$;
(D) $S_{1}>S_{2}$, sometimes $S_{1}=S_{2}$, sometimes $S_{1}<S_{2}$.

